sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task (automatic, Gateway release serve phase), R1-R4, single-swamp-node, docs/reference/gateway-recovery.md#runtime-handoff; DECISIONS round 2 bug fix (terminate only when active, start only when not active; one test per branch); rule 7 (graceful handoff).
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 16, 20, 22 (no inspect step: cfgmgmt systemd writes the unit only on change, and guards pick the branch; one bounded wait).
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: gateway:release:handoff
  %% kind: process.horizon_handoff
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=caller tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>release runner
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Gateway Node<br/>Node 3 over ssh
  Note over GW: Release handoff, serve<br/>release 812 · phase serve
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `php artisan gateway:release:handoff --phase=serve`
  %%> - syntax: run by the Gateway release runner, not by the `orbit` CLI
  %%> When:
  %%> - in every Gateway release, after the switch to release 812
  %%> - Horizon was drained before the switch, so it is normally not active here
  %%> Who starts it:
  %%> - the release runner on the Gateway Node; no CLI or MCP call
  Note over GW: Render the Horizon unit<br/>Process 418 · task #5153
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - Process 418 is the `horizon` Process of the Gateway Node, Node 3
  %%> - no other change runs on Process 418; the Gateway holds one lock
  %%> Renders:
  %%> - the systemd unit `orbit-process-418-horizon.service` and its hash
  %%> - command `php artisan horizon`, directory `/home/orbit/orbit/apps/gateway`, user `orbit`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5153 recorded with the full intent; nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-process-horizon-handoff
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one run on Swamp serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 3's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - the unit content, its hash, the command, directory and user
  SW->>N: Publish, reload, enable<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 3 over `@swamp/ssh` from 209 with the official `@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd` behavior; nothing is copied to the Node
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the rendered unit with `unitFile`, reloads systemd and enables it
  %%> - an identical unit is left as it is, so no inspection runs first
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no start: the next step picks hand-off or start by a `guard`
  alt Horizon is active
    SW->>N: Hand off to new release<br/>ssh exec · horizon:terminate
    %%> When:
    %%> - a `guard` finds Horizon active at the step, so a rerun picks the right branch
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks Horizon to stop after its current jobs
    %%> - systemd starts it again from the new release
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the gentle action: no job is cut off
    %%> Fix:
    %%> - this guard was inverted; one test covers this branch
  else Horizon is not active
    SW->>N: Start Horizon<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd
    %%> When:
    %%> - a `guard` finds Horizon inactive, the normal case after the drain; `ensure: running`
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts the unit from the new release
    %%> Fix:
    %%> - this guard was inverted; one test covers this branch
  end
  SW->>N: Read Horizon state<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd.check
  %%> The pinned check reports drift without failing; the next native assertion enforces it.
  SW->>N: Check Horizon runs<br/>native assert
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the native assertion requires the enabled unit to be active after handoff or start
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the handoff only counts when Horizon runs again
  alt Horizon is active
    N-->>SW: active
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the unit is active
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>Process 418 active · unit hash
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 418 active, with the stored unit hash
    %%> - task #5153 succeeds; the release handoff goes on
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or not active
    %%> When:
    %%> - the unit does not verify, a command fails, or Horizon is not active at the end check
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark Process 418 failed<br/>handoff fails · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 418 marked failed; task #5153 fails
    %%> - the release handoff reports the failure; the release failure rules apply
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a published unit stays; the old unit is not restored
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the handoff again after a fix; an unchanged unit is skipped, and Horizon starts only when it is not active
  end
